    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000064",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Once the ***E***<sup>ꝋ </sup>of a half-cell is known, the **potential difference** or **voltage** or** emf** of an **electrochemical cell **made up of any two half-cells can be calculated",
    "reading_order" : 64,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000065",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "These could be **any** half-cells and neither have to be a standard hydrogen electrode",
    "reading_order" : 65,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000066",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The **standard cell potential (***E*<sub>*cell*</sub><sup>ꝋ</sup>) can be calculated by **subtracting **the **less** **positive** *E*<sup>ꝋ </sup>from the **more positive ***E*<sup>ꝋ </sup>value",
    "reading_order" : 66,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000067",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The half-cell with the more positive *E*<sup>ꝋ </sup>value will be the **positive** pole",
    "reading_order" : 67,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000068",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "By convention this is shown on the right hand side in a conventional cell diagram, so is termed ** *****E***<sub>***right***</sub><sup>**ꝋ**</sup>",
    "reading_order" : 68,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000069",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The half-cell with the less positive *E*<sup>ꝋ </sup>value will be the **negative **pole",
    "reading_order" : 69,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000070",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "By convention this is shown on the left hand side in a conventional cell diagram, so is termed ** *****E***<sub>***left***</sub><sup>**ꝋ**</sup>",
    "reading_order" : 70,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000071",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "***E***<sub>***cell***</sub><sup>**ꝋ**</sup>** = *****E***<sub>***right***</sub><sup>**ꝋ **</sup>**- *****E***<sub>***left***</sub><sup>**ꝋ   **</sup>",
    "reading_order" : 71,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000072",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Since oxidation is always on the left and reduction on the right, you can also use this version",
    "reading_order" : 72,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
